     <section xml:id="sec-examples"> 
      <title>Examples</title>
      <slide>
        <title>Newton's law of cooling</title>
        <p>
        The time rate of change of the temperature of a body is proportional to the difference between the body's temperature and the temperature of the surrounding medium.
        </p>
      </slide>
      <slide>
        <title>Torricelli's law</title>
        <p>
        The time rate of change of the volume of water draining from a tank is proportional to the square root of the depth of water in the tank.
        </p>
        <p>We can find a general equation and also a common special case of a right cylindrical tank.</p>
      </slide>
      <slide>
        <title>Population growth</title>
        <p>
          A simplistic model of population growth when birth and death rates are constant is that the time rate of change of the population is proportional to the current population.  
        </p>
        <p>If we further know that the population at 0 hours is 1000 bacteria and that the population at 1 hour is 2000 bacteria, how can we make the differential equation and its solution more specific to this particular scenario?</p>
      </slide>
    </section>

     <section xml:id="sec-practice"> 
      <title>In-class practice</title>
      <slide>
        <title>IC-1</title>
        <p>
          Verify by substitution that both <m>y_1=\cos(x) -\cos(2x)</m> and <m>y_2=\sin(x)-\cos(2x)</m> are solutions to the differential equation <m>y^{\prime\prime}+y=3\cos(2x)</m>. <!--EPC4 1.1.8-->
        </p>
      </slide>
      <slide>
        <title>IC-2</title>
        <p>
          For what values of <m>r</m> is <m>y=e^{r x}</m> a solution of <m>4y^{\prime\prime}=y</m>? <!--EPC 1.1.14-->
        </p>
      </slide>
      <slide>
        <title>IC-3</title>
        <p>
          Write a differential equation describing a graph whose tangent to the graph at point <m>(x,y)</m> intercepts the <m>x</m>-axis at the point <m>\left(\frac{x}{2},0\right)</m>. <!--EPC 1.1.28 -->
        </p>
      </slide>
      <slide>
        <title>IC-4</title>
        <p>
         Write a differential equation modeling the information that the acceleration <m>\frac{d v}{d t}</m> of a Lamborghini is proportional to the difference between 250km/h and the velocity of the car. <!--EPC 1.1.34-->
        </p>
      </slide>
    </section>

